 "level_notes": {
  "0": "SNOBOL4 was implemented in the SIL macro language ('The Macro Implementation of SNOBOL4'); CSNOBOL4 (Phil Budne) is a C build of that SIL code, and SPITBOL (now spitbol/x64 on GitHub) is an independent, much faster compiler written in the MINIMAL machine-independent assembly language.",
  "1": "No ANSI/ISO standard; 'The SNOBOL4 Programming Language' (2nd ed., 1971, the 'Green Book') is the definition, preceded by the 1964 JACM paper on SNOBOL.",
  "3": "Rosetta Code reports 'blocked' to automated checkers."
 },
